{"id": "EUVD-2026-103952", "enisaUuid": "f41e2fc6-97f8-3167-99e7-d16d538a81c7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: handle empty FILS association request payload\n\nfils_encrypt_assoc_req() accepts a (Re)Association Request frame whose\nlast element is the FILS Session element.  crypt_len is then zero and\naes_siv_encrypt() is called with an empty plaintext.\n\nkmemdup() returns ZERO_SIZE_PTR for a zero-length allocation, so the\nunconditional sg_init_one() puts an invalid page into the scatterlist.\nWith CONFIG_DEBUG_SG this triggers a kernel BUG in sg_set_buf();\nwithout the debug check the bogus page is handed to the crypto backend.\n\nAES-SIV is defined for empty plaintext and the S2V result is then the\ncomplete output, so handle this case before the CTR step, which has\nnothing to encrypt.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b1e4a7eeb6a301ee33bd318982927cbdbae9f36", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f5b62f6534d336a62fdb9e88b186dd70b4323ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/452f1c9b76f7a122bbc4630b9691bda4809677c4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/20f939b0c151d1d28e6b62a76b2454fa6fe877f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5bfd4b0b40b79781d900cb2f7da0685070f53c67"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98698", "GHSA-873v-4wm2-m9cr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cd818dd-2de0-3332-ab5c-a8a9b2cfb9e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "26ae2524-0fea-34b5-bd9d-0917057ff94a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3e6a92d8-73cd-3bc2-ac0c-17d12b6cc89a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "39404feee691a2dc524a629ed6eb5cfe5d8898d1 <20f939b0c151d1d28e6b62a76b2454fa6fe877f2"}, {"id": "53216983-82fc-300d-afbd-150b28c00d8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "5e18d076-5475-3d72-8e0f-0204dcdf7c58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "39404feee691a2dc524a629ed6eb5cfe5d8898d1 <452f1c9b76f7a122bbc4630b9691bda4809677c4"}, {"id": "6ae8a0a2-0195-34c8-b776-f705dc8654d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "79bf97a1-66b2-3ad5-a782-6d1470016af8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "39404feee691a2dc524a629ed6eb5cfe5d8898d1 <2f5b62f6534d336a62fdb9e88b186dd70b4323ef"}, {"id": "8ed04a26-5a57-3e61-b0a0-90ef6272db56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.10"}, {"id": "90a4a09a-50e8-3f53-ac66-c7249eb91605", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "39404feee691a2dc524a629ed6eb5cfe5d8898d1 <0b1e4a7eeb6a301ee33bd318982927cbdbae9f36"}, {"id": "acf485c1-c0da-35ce-a2e0-3d1ecea1ed8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "c69df39b-1451-3a0f-ab34-ee6e64c50849", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "d0c60c2c-fbf0-3048-9483-0bb5e33920f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "39404feee691a2dc524a629ed6eb5cfe5d8898d1 <5bfd4b0b40b79781d900cb2f7da0685070f53c67"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "afcaac91-328e-3d7a-a884-9f72b19ca642", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}